# Shape-based ignore: deny everything, then allow sources and docs back.
#
# This inverts the usual approach deliberately. Listing build output by
# name meant every new executable was committable until someone
# remembered to add it, which is how seven binaries ended up tracked.
# Here anything not explicitly allowed below is ignored, so object
# files, assembly, preprocessed output and extensionless executables
# stay out with no maintenance.
#
# Adding a new kind of source file means adding one line here.

# Deny everything...
*

# ...but descend into directories. Without this git never recurses, and
# nothing inside week0/, week1/ etc. could be allowed back.
!*/

# C sources and headers
!*.c
!*.h

# Build and helper scripts
!Makefile
!*.sh

# Answer sheets, notes and documentation
!*.md

# This file
!.gitignore

# Per-week scratch space: classwork practice, test code, experiments.
# Never submitted. Listed last so it overrides the allow rules above.
practice/
